<h1 align="center">Solver-in-the-Loop: A Survey of Symbolic Solver Integration in Large Language Model Reasoning</h1>

<p align="center">
  Yishuai Geng · Guohui Xiao · Guilin Qi · Tianxing Wu · Peifeng Zhang
</p>

<div align="center">

**@PAPER_LINKS@ · [Study catalogue](papers/catalogue.md) · [Figures](assets/README.md) · [Citation](#citation)**

</div>

This survey examines how large language models use symbolic solvers across **@STUDIES@ studies** and **@REPORTS@ reports**. Eligible studies were first reported between January 2020 and October 2026. The framework distinguishes symbolic solving, verification, diagnosis and repair, search control, and learning supervision as five overlapping roles for solver outputs. Within-study comparisons examine how outcomes vary with the task, model, and computational budget.

